# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore — files git should NOT track.   (guide step 41 — 30 seconds)
# ==============================================================================
# Each line is a pattern. Matching files are invisible to `git status` /
# `git add`. A leading `!` re-includes something an earlier pattern excluded.
# ==============================================================================

# Build output
# Maven writes compiled classes and jars to <module>/target/. Always rebuildable,
# so never committed.
target/
# Exception: the Maven Wrapper's jar (if a project uses ./mvnw). This project
# has no .mvn folder, so this line currently does nothing.
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# IDE
# Editor/IDE project files (IntelliJ, VS Code, Eclipse) and Vim swap files.
# Personal to each developer, so not shared.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.settings/
.project
.classpath
*.swp
*.swo

# Environment and secrets
# .env holds OPENAI_API_KEY etc., which docker-compose reads. NEVER commit it:
# a key pushed to a public repo gets scraped and abused within minutes.
.env
# Presumably a file where the author kept an API key at some point.
api.txt

# OS
# macOS Finder and Windows Explorer metadata files.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
# Any *.log file. (Spring Shell's command-history file, if it is named
# spring-shell.log as I believe it is, is covered by this too.)
*.log
